"total_blocking":0},"body":"I want to rewrite my dataproviders from yii1 to yii2.\n\nThis is my test code\n\n``` php\n public function actionTest()\n    {\n        $query = new Query;\n        // $query->select(['p.id', 'p.title', 'GROUP_CONCAT(t.tag SEPARATOR \", \") AS tag'])\n        $query->select('p.id, p.title, GROUP_CONCAT(t.tag SEPARATOR \", \") AS tag')\n            ->from('posts p')\n            ->leftJoin('blog_tags t', 'p.id=t.post_id')\n            ->where('p.id = 1')\n            ->groupBy('p.id,');\n\n\n\n        $dataProvider = new ActiveDataProvider([\n            'query' => $query,\n\n            'pagination' => [\n                'pageSize' => 10,\n            ],\n        ]);\n\n\n\n        return $this->render('index', [\n                'dataProvider' => $dataProvider,\n        ]);\n    }\n```\n\nThat produce the following error:\n\n```\nSQLSTATE[42000]: Syntax error or access violation: 1064 You have an error in your SQL syntax; check the manual that corresponds to your MySQL server version for the right syntax to use near 'tag` FROM `posts` `p` LEFT JOIN `blog_tags` `t` ON p.id=t.post_id WHERE p.id = 1' at line 1\nThe SQL being executed was: SELECT `p`.`id`, `p`.`title`, GROUP_CONCAT(t.tag SEPARATOR \", `\")` AS `tag` FROM `posts` `p` LEFT JOIN `blog_tags` `t` ON p.id=t.post_id WHERE p.id = 1 GROUP BY `p`.`id` LIMIT 10\n```\n\nBy all other separators except the comma it works.\nIt also works with an array as $query->select([])\n\nI have many DAO sql strings in my yii1 project.\nIs it possible to provide a SqlDataProvider how in yii1.\n","closed_by":{"login":"qiangxue","id":993322,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5MzMyMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/993322?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/qiangxue","html_url":"https://github.com/qiangxue","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qiangxue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/qiangxue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://a